\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{The velocity near an equilibrium}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The Morris–Lecar velocity of \ref{fnip-0005} vanishes at the
[equilibrium](fnip-0014)
#{(V_{R},n_{R})}
of the Hopf column at #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60}, and at
#{(V_{*},n_{*})}
when #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100}. A nearby state is that equilibrium
plus a displacement #{y}. The velocity there is, to first order, the
derivative of the velocity applied to #{y}.}

\p{The derivative is a constant matrix. Its eigenvalues decide whether
a solution of the resulting linear equation approaches the equilibrium,
leaves it, or turns as it does so.}
